# Who reviews what.
#
# There is one maintainer: `git shortlog -sn` puts @divshekhar at ~2000 of the ~2200 commits, and
# every other name is a contributor rather than a reviewer. This file does not change who that is —
# it changes whether GitHub knows. Without it a PR opens with NO requested reviewer, so 24 of the
# 42 open PRs were green, mergeable, and waiting on a review nobody had been asked for.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all is FIRST and the per-area lines below it are the
# ones GitHub actually reports. They are spelled out per package and per app on purpose: the day a
# second maintainer takes one area, the change is one owner on one line, not a new file.

